#' Simulated Indian horticultural exports by product and destination
#'
#' Simulated annual exports of four Indian horticultural product groups to
#' eight destination markets, with world imports of each product by each
#' destination. The data are **synthetic**, generated by
#' `data-raw/make_data.R` for illustration; they are not official trade
#' statistics.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 448 rows and 6 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{year}{Year, 2010-2023.}
#'   \item{product}{`"mango"`, `"grapes"`, `"pomegranate"` or
#'     `"processed"` (processed fruit and vegetable products).}
#'   \item{destination}{Destination market.}
#'   \item{export_value}{Exports from India, USD million.}
#'   \item{export_quantity}{Export quantity, tonnes.}
#'   \item{world_import}{World imports of the product by the destination,
#'     USD million.}
#' }
#' @source Simulated.
"hort_exports"

#' Simulated total exports of India and the world
#'
#' Synthetic annual totals used with [hort_exports] to compute revealed
#' comparative advantage. Not official statistics.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 14 rows and 3 columns: `year`,
#'   `india_total_exports` and `world_total_exports` (USD million).
#' @source Simulated.
"trade_totals"

#' Simulated monthly exchange rates of the Indian rupee
#'
#' Synthetic monthly exchange rates (Indian rupees per unit of foreign
#' currency), January 2014 to December 2023. AED and SAR follow their US
#' dollar pegs. Not official statistics.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 120 rows and 8 columns: `date`, `USD`, `EUR`,
#'   `GBP`, `AED`, `SAR`, `BDT` and `RUB`.
#' @source Simulated.
"fx_rates"

#' Simulated monthly grape export and domestic prices
#'
#' Synthetic monthly export unit values and domestic wholesale prices of
#' grapes (INR per kg), January 2012 to December 2023, generated as a
#' cointegrated pair with faster adjustment when domestic prices are above
#' their long-run relationship. Not official statistics.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 144 rows and 3 columns: `date`,
#'   `export_unit_value` and `domestic_price`.
#' @source Simulated.
"grape_prices"
